---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site';

const updated = '28 November 2026';
const contact = 'gfxindia@gmail.com';
---

<Base title={`Privacy · ${site.name}`} description="What Movie Monkey does with your data: nothing is collected about you.">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-[720px] px-6 pt-16 pb-28 sm:pt-24">
    <p class="text-[13px] font-semibold tracking-[0.12em] text-accent-strong uppercase">Privacy</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 font-display text-[36px] leading-[1.08] font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-balance sm:text-[44px]">
      Nothing is collected about you.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-[15px] text-ink-3">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <div class="prose-mm mt-10">
      <p>
        Movie Monkey is free and has no accounts, no ads and no analytics in its apps. This page says exactly what
        leaves your devices and why. It covers the Mac app, the TV app (including the LG TV app) and this website.
      </p>

      <h2>The Mac app</h2>
      <p>
        Your library stays on your Mac. That means the folders you add, what Movie Monkey recognises in them, what
        you've watched and where you stopped, all kept in Movie Monkey's own folder on your Mac.
      </p>
      <p>
        To recognise a film or show, Movie Monkey sends the name and year it reads from a file name (for example
        “Heat 1995”) to <a href="https://www.themoviedb.org/privacy-policy">TMDB</a> and{' '}
        <a href="https://www.tvmaze.com/site/privacy">TVMaze</a>, and downloads posters and artwork from them. Like
        any website you visit, they see your Mac's internet address when it asks. Nothing else about you or your
        files is sent. If you choose to watch a trailer, it opens on YouTube in your browser.
      </p>

      <h2>Watch on TV</h2>
      <p>
        When you switch on Watch on TV, your Mac shares your library on your home network, and only with TVs you
        pair using a code shown on your Mac. Videos go straight from your Mac to your TV over your home network. They
        don't go through the internet, and they don't go through us.
      </p>

      <h2>The TV app</h2>
      <p>
        The TV app, including Movie Monkey for LG TVs, talks only to Movie Monkey on your computer, over your home
        network. To find your computer, it asks your TV for its address on your home network and then checks the
        other addresses on that network for Movie Monkey. That check stays inside your home network; nothing about it
        is stored or sent anywhere else. The app keeps your computer's address and its pairing key on your TV, so it
        can reconnect.
      </p>
      <p>
        <b>Sample films.</b> If you choose to try the sample films, the app loads them from this website, streams
        the films from the <a href="https://archive.org/about/terms.php">Internet Archive</a> (archive.org) and
        their artwork from TMDB. Those services see your TV's internet address when it asks. Where you stopped in
        them and what you've marked as watched are kept on your TV only.
      </p>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        This website is hosted by Vercel and uses{' '}
        <a href="https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/privacy-policy">Vercel Web Analytics</a> to count page visits. It
        uses no cookies and doesn't identify you or follow you to other sites.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>Movie Monkey doesn't collect anything about anyone, children included.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If this ever changes, this page will say so, with a new date at the top.</p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Write to <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>, or open an issue on{' '}
        <a href={`${site.github}/issues`}>GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose-mm {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .prose-mm :global(p + p) {
    margin-top: 1em;
  }
  .prose-mm :global(h2) {
    margin-top: 2.2em;
    margin-bottom: 0.6em;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .prose-mm :global(a) {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--line-strong);
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }
  .prose-mm :global(a:hover) {
    text-decoration-color: var(--ink);
  }
  .prose-mm :global(b) {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
